From c0916096b2921a1021fa0bbde8bc0782b7eec937 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:15:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] perf(worker): eliminate decode-step redundant H2D transfers,
 UVA copies, and eager ATen ops

Upstream base: 1107 vLLM patch head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488 (tree ed1bdb7a7684da33d403a055521ac0c4dd7ca670).

Rationale:
On every steady-state speculative decode step in GPUModelRunner, several host-to-device DMA transfers, UVA buffer rotations, and eager PyTorch ATen kernel launches ran unconditionally even when their outputs were immediately overwritten or unused:
1. GPUModelRunner.add_requests() called self.sampler.apply_staged_writes() outside the if scheduler_output.scheduled_new_reqs: guard, rotating and copying 15 UvaBackedTensors and checking 7 StagedWriteTensors on every decode step even though sampler.add_request() only runs for new requests.
2. BlockTables.apply_staged_writes() unconditionally called fused_writer.apply() (which gathers every group's staged lists before finding them empty) and num_blocks.copy_to_uva() (a UVA buffer rotation and copy) on every decode step even when no request crossed a KV block boundary (overwrite=False and empty block_ids).
3. In GPUModelRunner.prepare_inputs(), when adaptive_verification is enabled, async_tensor_h2d(cu_num_logits_np) and async_tensor_h2d(query_start_loc_np) allocated pinned host memory and launched two H2D cudaMemcpyAsync transfers whose destination tensors were immediately overwritten on-device by adaptive_verification.reallocate_drafts() (tilelang_inputs.adaptive_offsets).
4. In GPUModelRunner.sample_tokens() before speculator.propose(), clamping num_rejected by _dead_row_cut (repeated in both model_runner.py and OnlineAcceptanceEstimator.step) and masking CopyDrafter slots via torch.where(copy_drafter.int_state[idx_mapping, 1] > 0, -1, idx_mapping) launched 8 eager ATen kernels and 8 temporary GPU allocations on main_stream, and adaptive_verification.get_verified_draft_counts() was called a second time before copy_drafter.prepare_alloc(). In DraftModelSpeculator._copy_request_inputs(), idx_mapping[num_reqs:].fill_(-1) also launched a 0-element fill kernel when num_reqs == max_num_reqs.

Fix all of these per-step decode overheads:
1. Guard self.sampler.apply_staged_writes() under if scheduler_output.scheduled_new_reqs: in GPUModelRunner.add_requests().
2. Track a _dirty flag on BlockTables, set by append_block_ids when it stages a write or changes num_blocks, so a step with nothing to publish (every append overwrite=False with empty new_block_ids, and no write staged on a table directly) skips fused_writer.apply() and num_blocks.copy_to_uva(). apply_staged_writes() still applies a write staged on a table directly, outside append_block_ids, as before: the skip is taken only when there is nothing staged at all (the fused staged-write and declared-call coverage tests of tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_tilelang_inputs.py stage that way).
3. Skip the redundant cu_num_logits and query_start_loc async_tensor_h2d() transfers in GPUModelRunner.prepare_inputs() when adaptive_verification is active.
4. Fuse optional dead_row_cut clamping (HAS_DEAD_ROW_CUT) and CopyDrafter slot masking (HAS_COPY_STATE) directly into OnlineAcceptanceEstimator._accumulate_kernel, reuse num_verified_draft_tokens for copy_drafter.prepare_alloc(), and guard idx_mapping[num_reqs:].fill_(-1) with if num_reqs < self.max_num_reqs:.

Quality implications:
None. All tensor values, acceptance-estimator IRLS accumulators, and speculative verification outputs are bit-exact with the baseline.

Tests:
- pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_acceptance_estimator.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_copy_drafts.py tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_block_table.py tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_model_runner_v2.py tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_input_batch_v2.py (219 passed, 1 skipped across 2 boots on sp5).
- tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_block_table.py::test_block_tables_apply_staged_writes_applies_writes_staged_on_a_table: a write staged on a table directly, outside append_block_ids, lands on the next apply_staged_writes().
- pytest tests/v1/worker/test_gpu_tilelang_inputs.py (682 passed, 1 skipped on sp8, on 1107 with candidate-47's 0762..0769 and this patch as 0766; with the first version of this patch, test_apply_fused_staged_writes and test_declared_calls_cover_the_call_sites failed).

Upstream status:
Local worker and speculative-decoding step-overhead optimization for GB10 clusters.
